      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hepatotoxicity is the most common cause of fulminant hepatic failure in the United States and the main indication for market withdrawal of drugs. This condition has been increasingly recognized as a problem of enormous medical, financial legal, and regulatory importance. It is in context of this heightened awareness of hepatotoxicity, particularly associated with new high profile drugs, that the authors reviews the published data regarding liver injury related to a novel group of asthma drugs."},
